=== NOTES / methodology ===
- Serve: Profile B on .1:8081 — YaRN 4x -> 1M max-model-len, nvfp4 KV cache, A4Q on, MTP-3,
  --enable-prefix-caching, --max-num-batched-tokens 4096 (chunked prefill). Single DGX Spark (GB10).
- "prompt_tok" = ACTUAL tokens (server usage.prompt_tokens via stream_options.include_usage), not a target.
- COLD by construction: a unique lead block per depth defeats prefix-cache reuse, so TTFT reflects a true
  first-touch prefill (worst case), not a cache hit.
- TTFT = time to first generated token = full prefill wall-clock. prefill tok/s = prompt_tok / TTFT.
- decode tok/s = 128 forced tokens (ignore_eos + min_tokens) so decode-at-depth is a clean, EOS-independent sample.
- passkey: a secret code embedded at ~60% depth; HIT = model retrieved it -> coherence/retrieval holds at depth.
- Cold prefill throughput falls steeply with context (1537 -> 355 tok/s @ 50K -> 500K); this is the O(n^2)
  attention prefill cost + 4096-chunked prefill. A genuine cold single-shot 1M prefill is ~70 min, which
  exceeded the 3600s client timeout on the first attempt -> re-measured with a 2h timeout in
  bench/context_sweep_1m.log. NOTE: real-world 1M use fills context incrementally (prefix caching reuses
  prior turns), so the cold single-shot number is the pessimistic bound, not the steady-state cost.
- FIRST-PASS CORRECTION: an earlier sweep sized prompts by chars (~4 chars/tok) and, without include_usage,
  logged the TARGET as prompt_tok. This filler tokenizes at ~6.9 chars/tok, so those prompts were ~57% of
  their labels (the "1M" run was really ~576K tokens). This v2 log fixes both (accurate tokens + real counts).

=== 1M point (resolved) ===
- Re-measure (context_sweep_1m.log): prompt_tok=986,108 | TTFT=1522.6s (25.4 min, 648 tok/s) | decode=5.1 tok/s | passkey=HIT.
- CAVEAT: this 648 tok/s is WARM, not cold. The v2 cold 1M attempt ran the full 60 min (02:30->03:30) and the
  server cached its prefill blocks before the client's 3600s timeout fired; the immediate re-measure (same unique
  prefix) therefore hit a warm prefix cache -> 648 tok/s is impossible for cold (it beats the 500K cold point).
- HONEST COLD 1M: ~60 min at ~274 tok/s (986,108 tok / ~3600s). That 274 tok/s sits exactly on the 50K->500K cold
  decline (1537->1119->611->355->~274), and it is why the first attempt hit the 3600s wall right at completion.
- REAL-WORLD 1M: warm/incremental (prefix caching reuses prior turns) ~= the 25.4 min / 648 tok/s figure.
- RETRIEVAL: passkey HIT at 986,108 tokens -> coherence/retrieval confirmed at ~1M (not just 500K).
